Apply SSML pitch changes in time for MBROLA voices.

With a normal eSpeak NG voice, a pitch change from SSML (for example
<prosody pitch="175%">) becomes an embedded command. DoEmbedded() puts it
in the wave command queue, and the wave generator applies it when it
reaches that point in the audio. That is right for eSpeak's own
synthesizer, which reads the pitch while it makes the sound.

MBROLA voices work differently. MbrolaTranslate() computes each
phoneme's pitch points (WritePitch() -> SetPitch2()) and sends them to
MBROLA as soon as the phoneme is translated. That happens before the
wave generator has taken the queued pitch command, so the phonemes the
change was meant for are already written with the old pitch. The change
lands afterwards, usually together with the command that undoes it.

The result in NVDA: "Capital pitch change percentage" does nothing,
because NVDA raises the pitch of a capital letter with a PitchCommand,
which the driver sends as <prosody pitch="...">. Pitch range and the
punctuation tone have the same problem. Worse, when MbrolaTranslate()
stops because the queue is full, the wave generator can apply a stale
pitch command in the middle of the clause and the rest of the clause is
spoken at the wrong pitch.

When an MBROLA voice is active, apply pitch, pitch range and tone
commands immediately in DoEmbedded(), the same way the speed command is
already handled, instead of queueing them. Normal eSpeak voices are not
affected. espeak_ng_Cancel() already restores the parameters, so a
cancelled utterance cannot leave the pitch raised.

diff --git a/src/libespeak-ng/synthesize.c b/src/libespeak-ng/synthesize.c
index 1ca14e1..bdf038d 100644
--- a/src/libespeak-ng/synthesize.c
+++ b/src/libespeak-ng/synthesize.c
@@ -1105,6 +1105,19 @@ void DoEmbedded(int *embix, int sourceix)
 		case EMBED_U: // play sound
 			DoMarker(espeakEVENT_PLAY, count_characters+1, 0, value); // always occurs at end of clause
 			break;
+		case EMBED_P: // pitch
+		case EMBED_R: // pitch range
+		case EMBED_T: // tone for announcing punctuation
+#if USE_MBROLA
+			if (mbrola_name[0] != 0) {
+				// MBROLA voices get their pitch when each phoneme is translated
+				// (WritePitch() in synth_mbrola.c), long before wavegen would
+				// apply a queued command. Apply the change now.
+				SetEmbedded(command, value);
+				break;
+			}
+#endif
+			// fall through
 		default:
 			DoPause(10, 0); // ensure a break in the speech
 			wcmdq[wcmdq_tail][0] = WCMD_EMBEDDED;
